<section class="content-section"><div class="shell content-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Sector treatment</div><h2>Depth follows evidence.</h2><p>Sector language supports the client problem. It does not replace authority, scope or evidence assessment.</p></div><div class="indexed-list"><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">01</span><div><h3>Problem-led triage</h3><p>Start with the business problem, trigger and desired outcome.</p></div></div><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">02</span><div><h3>Operating context</h3><p>Keep Industry, Activity and Operating Environment distinct rather than using a broad sector label as a shortcut.</p></div></div><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">03</span><div><h3>Jurisdiction and authority</h3><p>Identify where specialised jurisdiction or sector authority would need to be established before consulting proceeds.</p></div></div><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">04</span><div><h3>Fit decision</h3><p>Proceed, request more discovery or say not a fit. No automatic specialist claim.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
